Patashu wrote:
> If I were to complete the game with a conduct outside of those the game
> tracks, what would be an interesting one to try?

Well, most of the extra conducts people come up with are mind-blowingly
difficult. However, you can always set yourself some small but
satisfying challenge, like ascending with all nine Nazgul rings
(they'll be safe away from the mortals!), or ascending with obscene
amounts of gems and riches (hereafter known as the DeathOnAStick
challenge, or DOAS for short[1]).

Fascinating but difficult conducts include:
 * beach-bum (on #nethack the other day, someone mentioned this conduct
in which the only armour you're allowed are Hawaiian shirts.)
 * inventoryless (urk! There is a thread in this group about this one)
 * Zen (play blindfolded, except for doing the Invocation;
traditionally you play as a samurai since they can start with a
blindfold. This is about the only instance where startscumming is not
frowned upon.)
 * magicless (I don't know if this has been proposed before... rings,
amulets, scrolls, spellbooks are forbidden to use. I can't think of a
neat way to forbid *all* kinds of enchanted item, especially
considering that the NetHack universe apparently doesn't cleanly
discriminate.)



[1] Speaking of which, someone proposed a tribute patch:
"DeathOnAStick's ghost floats through the wall. DeathOnAStick's ghost
picks up 43 rocks. DeathOnAStick's ghost collapses in a sobbing heap."



